# ICxA Protocol Licensing — Proposed Terms

**DRAFT FOR ICxA APPROVAL — NOT AN EFFECTIVE LICENSE**

This draft describes ICxA's proposed licensing model for OCRS and OAP. It is not a grant of permission and must not be represented as a currently effective license.

## Proposed free evaluation rights

Subject to the final executed terms, ICxA intends to permit individuals and organizations to access, copy and run the protocol reference implementations, schemas, tests and examples solely for internal, noncommercial research, development, interoperability experiments and evaluation.

## Commercial and public use

A separate written commercial license from ICxA, associated with an eligible active ICxA Corporate Membership, is required before commercial use, production deployment, providing services or software to customers, or public distribution of implementations or derivatives covered by these terms. Corporate Membership alone does not automatically grant a license: the applicable written license must be issued.

## Rights reserved

No trademark, logo, endorsement, certification, official conformity claim, patent or normative specification republication rights are granted by this draft. Official ICxA certification and marks require separate authorization.

## Publication conditions

Before this proposal becomes effective, ICxA must approve the final license text, confirm ownership and contributor permissions, define covered materials and prohibited uses precisely, and publish the effective date and commercial licensing process. Open-source licensing terminology should not be used for a commercial-use-restricted license.

For licensing enquiries, consult ICxA's official website at https://icxa.net/.
